<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 63–12 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa was a Roman general and statesman, the closest friend, son-in-law and chief lieutenant of Augustus. He commanded the fleets that won at Naulochus in 36 BCE and Actium in 31 BCE, ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars">Cantabrian Wars</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> in 19 BCE and built widely, including the first Pantheon in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emerita-augusta">Emerita Augusta</a> was dedicated in his name around 16–15 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marcus-vipsanius-agrippa.jpg" alt="Marcus Vipsanius Agrippa" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Agrippa_Gabii_Louvre_Ma1208.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
